        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "05392fad-8827-520c-9b31-b74cd6138162",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alexander Borodin\n- Works: Baubles, Bangles, & Beads; String Quartet in D\n- Topics: musical adaptation; Russian Romantic music\n\nFacts:\n- Alexander Porfiryevich Borodin was a Russian Romantic composer of Georgian origin, and he was also a doctor and chemist.\n- Alexander Borodin lived from 12 November 1833 to 27 February 1887.\n- The song \"Baubles, Bangles, & Beads\" used a melody based on Alexander Borodin's works.\n- In \"Baubles, Bangles, & Beads,\" the melody was based specifically on the second theme of the second movement of Alexander Borodin's \"String Quartet in D.\"",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "5c26a6d1-ad72-526c-86f4-62699810fb24",
        "text": "Page: Baubles, Bangles, &amp; Beads. Sentence: Like all the music in that show, the melody was based on works by Alexander Borodin, in this case the second theme of the second movement of his \"String Quartet in D.\"\nPage: Alexander Borodin. Sentence: Alexander Porfiryevich Borodin (Russian: Алекса́ндр Порфи́рьевич Бороди́н ; ] , 12 November 183327 February 1887) was a Russian Romantic composer of Georgian origin, as well as a doctor and chemist.",
